    "narrative": "For Ghost Ride the WHIP today, the offensive engine is anchored by **Corbin Carroll** (80.77) and **Josh Naylor** (72.66), who represent our highest-ceiling plays. **Corbin Carroll** benefits from a massive matchup against Jose Quintana, whose 5.24 xERA is the most exploitable target on the slate; his projected efficiency is bolstered by an elite 0.374 xwOBA. Similarly, **Josh Naylor** finds himself in an ideal spot hitting 3rd against Seth Lugo. While Lugo has respectable stuff, the data suggests **Josh Naylor**\u2019s combination of order security and positive platoon dynamics makes him a pillar for our run and RBI production. **James Wood** (71.88) also warrants high-leverage expectations, as his #1 spot in the lineup against the vulnerable Mart\u00edn P\u00e9rez offers significant base-clearing potential.\n\nThe most difficult roster decision involved keeping **Jose Caballero** on the bench. Despite his utility profile and the +2% boost provided by his ability to exploit slow pitcher deliveries\u2014critical for our focus on scarce SB totals\u2014his 44.46 score couldn't overcome the efficiency of our starters. His platoon disadvantage against Drew Rasmussen and the dampening effect of \"Wind In\" conditions ultimately pushed him behind the production floor of players like **Cole Young** (49.87) and **Dalton Rushing** (49.77). We are monitoring the status of **Brice Turang** and **Dalton Rushing** closely, as both are currently \"Lineup Pending.\" **Brice Turang** faces a steep challenge against the elite arsenal of Yoshinobu Yamamoto, and if his confirmed lineup position drops, we may see his already volatile 47.97 efficiency rating slide further into the sub-40 danger zone. \n\nRounding out the lineup, **Zach McKinstry** (64.69) and **Gabriel Moreno** (63.00) provide excellent value through park-adjusted and skill-matchup metrics. **Zach McKinstry** receives a massive 16% park boost, suggesting he could be the dark horse for a multi-hit performance against Young. While **Vinnie Pasquantino** (59.51) and **Tyler Soderstrom** (59.88) sit just on the cusp of the \"Strong\" 60+ tier, their consistent contact profiles against their respective right-handed matchups should stabilize our AVG category. We remain vigilant on weather and confirmed lineups, particularly regarding the potential for late-game defensive substitutions that could limit the plate appearances for **Dalton Rushing** and **Austin Riley**.",
